# Repot export

Generated by Repot 0.1.0 on 2026-11-02 10:00 UTC

Source: macOS -> Target: Linux (Debian/Ubuntu)

Review these files before restoring. Install the required package and version managers first.

## Restore

### Brewfile

```bash
brew bundle --file=Brewfile
```

### apt-packages.txt

```bash
xargs -a apt-packages.txt sudo apt-get install -y
```

### dnf-packages.txt

```bash
sudo dnf install -y $(cat dnf-packages.txt)
```

### pacman-packages.txt

```bash
sudo pacman -S --needed - < pacman-packages.txt
```

### .tool-versions

```bash
mise install # or asdf install
```

### npm-global.txt

```bash
xargs npm install -g < npm-global.txt
```

### pnpm-global.txt

```bash
xargs pnpm add -g < pnpm-global.txt
```

### pipx.txt

```bash
xargs -n1 pipx install < pipx.txt
```

### cargo.txt

```bash
xargs -n1 cargo install < cargo.txt
```

### vscode-extensions.txt

```bash
xargs -n1 code --install-extension < vscode-extensions.txt
```

### cursor-extensions.txt

```bash
xargs -n1 cursor --install-extension < cursor-extensions.txt
```

### Other runtimes

```bash
rustup toolchain install stable
```

### Config files

Back up existing destination files before copying.

| Source | Destination |
| --- | --- |
| `files/home/.zshrc` | `~/.zshrc` |
| `files/home/.ssh/config` | `~/.ssh/config` |

OpenSSH rejects SSH files that others can write: if you create `~/.ssh`, run `chmod 700 ~/.ssh`, and run `chmod 600` on each file you copy into it.

### oh-my-zsh plugins

Install oh-my-zsh first: https://ohmyz.sh

```bash
git clone https://github.com/zsh-users/zsh-autosuggestions ~/.oh-my-zsh/custom/plugins/zsh-autosuggestions
```

## SSH keys

Copy these SSH keys yourself (Repot does not export keys):
  - the keys you use (default names: id_ed25519, id_ecdsa, id_rsa)
  Copy each key and its .pub file from your old machine into ~/.ssh, then run chmod 600 on the private keys.

Secret detection is pattern-based and may not catch every secret. Review all files before sharing.
